{
  "explanation": "The attacker originating from IP 141.98.11.62 executed a brute force attack against the SSH service on host app-02. The logs show repeated failed login attempts using common administrative and service accounts such as root, admin, postgres, and git, indicating an automated dictionary-style credential guessing attempt.",
  "mitre_tactic": "Credential Access",
  "recommended_actions": [
    "Block the source IP address 141.98.11.62 at the firewall or configure Fail2ban to automatically ban IPs with repeated authentication failures.",
    "Disable password-based authentication for SSH and enforce the exclusive use of SSH cryptographic keys.",
    "Disable direct root login via SSH by setting 'PermitRootLogin no' in the sshd_config file."
  ]
}
